m]pages, provenance links, Referenced By write-backs) keeps working [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]remove_agents_sync_import.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/remove_agents_sync_import.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ws[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-ws/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove ACE import surfaces[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]ace-import-ui[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ace-import-ui: delete the top-bar agents-sync badge, periodic status [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checks, cached-hood integration action, comprehensive-update AGENTS leg,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Update-panel Agents row, and the ace.agents_sync config section, keeping[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]only a publish-scoped manual sync action in the Updates pane.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rescope sase agent sync to publication[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-publish-only[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ace-import-ui[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-publish-only: strip the import pass from full sync, the commit-time [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publication hook, and the --check/--refresh status path, remove sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent retire-v1, and drop every import count and field from SyncOutcome,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ProjectSyncStatus, and the --json output.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One explicit purge for imported local state[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]purge-local-state[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-publish-only[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]purge-local-state: generalize the v1 forget-import cleanup into one [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]explicit command that purges all locally materialized imported state [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](artifacts, bundles, journals, caches, receipts, import-origin registry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows) plus a doctor check that reports leftovers.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Delete the import engine and v1 leg[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]delete-import-engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after purge-local-state[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]delete-import-engine: delete the v2 importer, incoming cache/detection, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]v1 integration modules, registry import mutations, forget-import [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command, and ACE incomplete-import visibility gates with their tests; [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]remove the v1_import_retired flag and close bead sase-wc; refresh shard [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timings.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drop orphaned Rust import APIs[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rust-core-cleanup[dim] · [dim][/dim]after delete-import-engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust-core-cleanup: remove sase-core identity and wire surface whose only[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]callers were the deleted Python import leg, keeping anything still [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]needed to read historical local state, and update bindings and parity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Docs, memory record, and final sweep[/bold #D7AFFF]                     